    {
      "reviewId": "Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21vd1gzb3pWbVYxTUcxdU9DMWxlR1JXTlROUU1rRRAB",
      "authorName": "Selina Loke",
      "starRating": 5,
      "reviewDate": "4 months ago",
      "localGuideInfo": "Local Guide · 138 reviews",
      "text": "Erhai Lake Park is a continuous long walk along the boardwalk that lined the shores of the lake in Dali, China. It starts at the pier of the North Gate at Shuanglang Ancient Town and circumvent through the famous S Bend area continueing to snake round the eco-park ending at the Park South Gate. Along the walk, at the other side across the lake runs the Cangsan Mountain Range. Its a beautiful sight to see the sunlight reflecting shimmering across the lake in the morning sun.",
      "scrapedAt": "2026-03-23T07:24:16.488Z"
    },
    {
      "reviewId": "Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xBMFNWOVpXbEl3Y1Zabk9YUnBORFV3VVc1UmJVRRAB",
      "authorName": "Jacob",
      "starRating": 5,
      "reviewDate": "2 months ago",
      "localGuideInfo": "Local Guide · 3K reviews",
      "text": "Erhai Park at the South Gate is a true gem in Dali. The long boardwalk along the lake offers a peaceful and scenic escape, perfect for a leisurely stroll or a bike ride. Renting a bicycle here is a must—it’s incredibly affordable and allows you to soak in the stunning views of the lake, charming shops, and traditional houses at your own pace. The area is dotted with picturesque spots, making it ideal for photography enthusiasts. I particularly loved the S Bend section, where the lake curves gracefully, creating a breathtaking vista. The atmosphere is relaxed and comfortable, even when it gets busier in the afternoon. Whether you're looking for a quiet morning ride or a lively afternoon exploration, this place delivers. The cherry blossoms nearby add a touch of magic, especially in the right season. Highly recommend for anyone visiting Dali!",
      "scrapedAt": "2026-03-23T07:24:16.490Z"
    },
    {
      "reviewId": "ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUR2Nl9UMk1BEAE",
      "authorName": "Fara Wahida",
      "starRating": 5,
      "reviewDate": "a year ago",
      "localGuideInfo": "3 reviews",
      "text": "Went here during early winter December 17th 2024. The weather was just nice 16 celcius, a bicycle ride is a must here. The place becomes more crowded after lunch hour but merrier. We found cherry blossow near this place as well. So preciously fresh🌸🌸🥰",
      "scrapedAt": "2026-03-23T07:24:16.490Z"
    },
    {
      "reviewId": "Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT210WlRHUlJZalJYVFZNd1gweHBXRVZOVlZGTmIzYxAB",
